#
# fivestar-loader --input-script: answers the first-run screens of an empty save folder unattended, up to the story
# load (docs/running.md#first-run-in-the-game). Only an empty save folder shows them; later boots skip them, so do not use
# this script then. The screen blocks wait for screens learned from your own frames
# (--screens, default %LOCALAPPDATA%\FiveStar\screens.txt). The first time, a block waits for a screen it does not
# know yet: press F8 when that screen shows, and the loader learns it and goes on. Presses are held 0.3 s: while
# pipelines compile the game can miss 0.2 s presses, and from about 0.5 s a held arrow repeats.
#
# Every press is a button of the virtual gamepad (PadA, PadDown, PadRight): the game took no scripted keyboard key.
# In boots from an empty folder 100 Space taps in 150 s and 16 Enter taps left the black screen standing, and 20
# Down taps left the focus of the legal screen on its first item; A passed the black screen and the option screens.
#
# Black "press a button" screen, logos, intro art and the first option screens (minimap, text size): an A tap every
# 1.5 s until the subtitles screen shows.
0 PadA hold 0.3 repeat 800 every 1.5

# Subtitles, Off by default: Right turns them on. Then the remaining option screens (brightness, controls notice): an
# A tap every 1.5 s until the legal screen shows. A tap does nothing on the legal screen while its Copyright item
# has the focus.
screen subtitles
1 PadRight hold 0.3
+1 PadA hold 0.3 repeat 800 every 1.5

# Legal notices, focus on Copyright: Down to the photosensitivity warning, which keeps the focus for 4 s, then
# Down every 1.5 s until Next has the focus.
screen legal
1 PadDown hold 0.3
+4.5 PadDown hold 0.3 repeat 20 every 1.5

# Legal notices, focus on Next: A until the terms screen shows (the first press after the focus moved can be
# dropped). The presses are 8 s apart: a press that lands on the terms screen before its block begins toggles a check
# box there, and the screen then no longer matches.
screen legal-next
1 PadA hold 0.3 repeat 3 every 8

# Privacy policy and terms of service: two check boxes that A toggles, then Confirm, which is enabled once both are
# checked. The focus starts on the first box. The policy text on the right scrolls by itself (63 to 132 cells changed in
# one boot), so the screen allows 160 changed cells; the legal screens are 233 and 256 cells away. Each step below
# repeats its press until a change block sees it take, so a press the game drops is pressed again and a press that took
# is not (a second A would clear the box). The changes are watched in the left panel only (cells 0-12 x 5-15, the
# boxes in column 1, rows 6-7 and 11-12, Confirm in rows 13-15), away from the scrolling text: a check mark changes a
# cell or two, a focus move about 30. A step that sees no change in 47 s goes on anyway, with a warning in the log.
#
# A select step tries A for 15 s, then the keyboard's Space for 15 s, then Enter; the first that takes ends the step.
#
# The block begins once the left half of the screen (the boxes, away from the scrolling text) has stayed still for 1 s,
# so the first press does not land while the screen still fades in.
screen terms 160 settle 1 settle-region 0 0 23 26
0.5 PadA hold 0.3 repeat 6 every 2.5
+15 Space hold 0.3 repeat 6 every 2.5
+15 Enter hold 0.3 repeat 6 every 2.5

# The privacy box is checked: Down moves the focus to the terms box (the right panel does not count).
change privacy-checked 1 region 0 5 3 13 timeout 47
1 PadDown hold 0.3 repeat 18 every 2.5

change terms-focused 6 region 0 5 12 15 timeout 47
1 PadA hold 0.3 repeat 6 every 2.5
+15 Space hold 0.3 repeat 6 every 2.5
+15 Enter hold 0.3 repeat 6 every 2.5

# Both boxes are checked: Down to Confirm, then select it until the story load shows.
change terms-checked 1 region 0 5 3 13 timeout 47
1 PadDown hold 0.3 repeat 18 every 2.5

change confirm-focused 6 region 0 5 12 15 timeout 47
1 PadA hold 0.3 repeat 6 every 2.5
+15 Space hold 0.3 repeat 6 every 2.5
+15 Enter hold 0.3 repeat 6 every 2.5

# The story load (a spinner on dark blue): nothing to press, the log names the time.
screen story-load
